- **Phase 2 audit gaps in `train_table_transformer.py` -- DONE 2026-05-07** --
  All three documented small-dataset levers are now wired through the CLI
  and `fine_tune_tatr()`:
  1. `--num-queries N` exposed. Default: keep the pretrained checkpoint's 15.
     Recommended for panel data: 15-20 per [DETR Issue #9](https://github.com/facebookresearch/detr/issues/9).
     When N differs from the checkpoint, query embeddings are re-initialised
     via `ignore_mismatched_sizes=True`.
  2. `--freeze-backbone-epochs N` added. Default: ~30% of `--epochs`
     (rounded). Pass 0 to disable. Implemented as a `TrainerCallback` that
     snapshots the backbone's original (partial-freeze) `requires_grad`
     state at training start, forces all backbone params off during the
     freeze window, then restores the snapshot -- preserves DETR's
     intentional freezing of early ResNet layers (`conv1`, `layer1`).
     Reference: [Dynamic Backbone Freezing (arxiv 2407.15143)](https://arxiv.org/html/2407.15143v4).
  3. `--hard-negatives-dir DIR` and `--hard-negatives-weight W` added.
     Negatives are loaded with empty target boxes (so the loss only fires
     against the no-object class) and concatenated with the positives via
     `WeightedRandomSampler` so each negative appears at `W * 1.0` the
     per-step rate of a positive (default `W=0.1`). Epoch length stays at
     the positive count so wall-clock time is comparable to a positives-only
     run. Implemented as a `Trainer` subclass overriding `_get_train_sampler`.
  Plan reference: `~/.cursor/plans/panel-detector-improvement-path_9fdbc9ca.plan.md`.

