  - **Diagnosis: mode collapse to 1 prediction per page.** Across
    all 15 runs (3 thresholds x 5 PDFs), the model produces *exactly
    1 prediction per page* at every threshold below 0.1, regardless
    of how many panels are actually there (GT counts: 6, 7, 8, 3,
    4). TATR's underlying DETR has 20 object queries (v6 retrain
    used `--num-queries 20`), but this model effectively fires only
    one. The most damning datapoint: on
    `Electrical_Takeoff_page7.pdf` (v4 = 1.00 mAP, the "easiest"
    of the 5), v6 produces a single wrong box. This is classic DETR
    mode collapse -- a known failure mode when training data is
    small or imbalanced, or when classification loss dominates bbox
    loss during early training.
  - **All four variants fail all three Phase 2 pass-criteria**
    (`mAP@0.5 >= 0.85 AND >= v4 baseline AND >= heuristic on >= 80% of PDFs`):
    v6 best @ 0.5 = 0.034, v6 final @ 0.5 = 0.000, v6 best @ 0.1
    = 0.059, v6 best @ 0.05 = 0.059. v4 (0.47) remains the best
    Table Transformer model.
  - **Recommended next step (UPDATED 2026-05-14 after training-time
    forensics)**: try a **recipe-fix retrain ("v7")** first; the
    Phase 3 (RF-DETR) escalation is now downgraded to a fallback if
    v7 also fails. See the "v6 root-cause investigation -- DONE
    2026-05-14" entry below: the training logs, hyperparameter
    diff against v4, and synthetic-positional-bias check together
    point at the v6 *training recipe* (not the architecture and not
    the dataset) as the cause of the mode collapse.
  - **Local artifacts** (all under `~/Documents/TableAnnotations/`):
    - `models_v6/best/` and `models_v6/checkpoint-3810/` are now
      available locally (transfer of ~440 MB total from Paperspace).
